  "visualReview": {
    "coverage": "Viewed all 64 pages and 8 covers in eight 3×3 contact sheets, then re-inspected corrected sheets. Selected full-size views: 0209 p08; 0210 p05 and p06; 0211 p06; 0212 p07 and p08; 0213 p06 and p08; 0214 p03, p06 and p08; 0215 p02, p07 and p08; 0216 p07 and p08.",
    "notes": [
      "0209: one square pumpkin bread is divided into equal halves. The chipmunk keeps the soft centre while the mole keeps the crust until they negotiate an exchange; small pieces are offered before the remaining portions are exchanged. The ending has two stacked empty plates and one small crumb at the mole’s nose. The seated chipmunk retains one continuous fluffy tail.",
      "0210: the rectangular cream carpet has four green corner fringes and one stitched face. It stays flowerless through jumping and rubbing; the first pink fabric flower appears where the tail tip touches it. The grandmother’s tail and the dancing younger mouse appear only in a framed memory. One shoe is removed first, then both shoes stand together outside the carpet as pink, yellow and blue cloth flowers appear.",
      "0211: the mouse stays on the wide plank deck beside the inner side of the right vine railing. The grass whisk is withdrawn, the curled leaf reveals a single dry bean pod, and the whole pod is removed before the wind is tested again. The leaf unfolds and the bridge’s two leaf ears settle as the mouse leaves with the bag.",
      "0212: the wooden pig stays approximately pear-sized, with three blue back spots and a green scarf. A twig orchard fails, a flat painting cannot yield fruit, and then folded card supports three doors attached along their top edges. The first opened door gives one strawberry to the pig’s forehooves while the other two doors stay shut. The last page has three open doors and three empty dishes.",
      "0213: one red roof moves from the fairy’s hands to the castle and then back into the box. The unfinished castle has no face and is dismantled before the long creature is completed. The creature has exactly six short block legs, one square head and one orange back block; it gains a face only once completed. The white-capped ladybug rests on the orange block at the end.",
      "0214: the ray kite has one continuous blue cloth tail through the tight, loosening and straightened stages. On the table the kite lies flat, the upset girl has tears, and the hands relax before the next attempt. The hanging kite connects to a reachable low window hook; the closed lower pane remains visible and the final tail touches the girl’s hand. White socks and brown shoes remain in seated and standing poses.",
      "0215: the cloud ball has no face. Its shape changes from round to flattened, then dented, partially restored and finally round. The pig admits what happened, waits with the sheep, returns the round ball and sits on the grass to continue playing. One food box remains nearby and the pig’s white bean pocket and sheep’s pale purple scarf stay consistent.",
      "0216: the rooftop is enclosed by a complete railing. The teal cabinet has two curved brass handles and one round mouth; it opens only after the towel answer. The towel, tablecloth and plate stay stored while the green picnic mat is removed. Exactly two pointed date pastries remain in the ending: one whole on the plate and one with a single tip bitten off in the mouse’s hands."
    ],
    "limits": "Simplified original vector picture-book style. Contact sheets check composition and continuity; selected pages are enlarged. This review does not include bitmap painting, audio QA, browser layout QA or child-user testing."
  },
